    "code_current_through_note": "eCode360 breadcrumb 'Code 2026-01-05'. Ord. No. 925, 928 and 929 (2026, zoning) are listed under New Laws and not yet codified.",
    "code_caution": "Three zoning amendments, Ord. No. 925 (2026-04-27), 928 (2026-06-22) and 929 (2026-09-28), are not yet in the online code. A search of their text finds no accessory dwelling, accessory apartment, in-law or granny wording, but Ord. No. 928 restates the single-family attached and duplex definitions and their parking. They were not read in full, so ask the Township about the duplex route.",
    "checks": [
      "The zoning code has no accessory dwelling unit, accessory apartment, in-law, ECHO or granny flat provision. A code search for those words and for caretaker, cottage, 'accessory unit' and 'living quarters' found none. The 2016 Comprehensive Plan recommends permitting ADUs, and a 2017 Zoning Hearing Board agenda lists a variance request for a second dwelling unit as a 'granny flat'",
      "Uses not listed for a district are not allowed: 'No building, structure or land shall be constructed or used for any purpose ... other than' the listed uses. 'All other uses' are a conditional use only in the IN district (440-402A, Figure 400.2)",
      "Not more than one detached principal building on a lot, except in a planned land development (440-402A)",
      "A duplex ('a single residential structure that is divided into two dwelling units each of which has a separate entrance') is a single-family attached dwelling. Single-family attached dwellings are permitted by right in MD, VR, TC, VC, MA.1, MA.2, WV and VB, and in the CR and MR overlays (440-301, Figure 400.2)",
      "MD allows at most 7 dwelling units per gross acre (Figure MD.2), and unit counts round up at 0.5 (440-402G(3)), so two units need about 9,334 sq ft (about 12,446 without rounding). LD allows 1.2 per acre, CL 2 per acre and RR one per 5 acres",
      "Accessory structures over 120 sq ft or 10 ft high meet the accessory setbacks, stay at least 5 ft from the house, and may not hold a use the district does not permit (440-501B, E, G)",
      "Existing lots without public sewer need a septic system approved by the Sanitary District and at least one acre. New lots must connect to public water and sewer (440-402H(2))",
      "Parking: 2 spaces per dwelling unit for single-family detached and attached dwellings (440-507, Figure 500.9)",
      "Limited lodging (short-term stays) is a permitted accessory use in most districts (Figure 400.2, 440-601)"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Peters Township Planning Department (peterstownship.com). Read on eCode360 (PE3557) in a browser, one print view at a time, on 2026-11-14. The Composite Land Use Chart (Figure 400.2) was read from screenshots of the HTML table. District pages read for LD, WP, CL, MD, RR and VR. Nonresidential, mixed-use and overlay district pages were not opened beyond the chart. A search snippet of the 2025-10-09 Planning Commission minutes (PDF, not opened) says a conversion of a single-family home to two units was found a permitted use because duplexes are single-family attached dwellings."
  },
